.RI "class \fBDeviceBuffer\fP"
.br
.RI "Represents a cache that can be shared with a hardware backend through \fBDeviceSharedBuffer<TDeviceSharedBackend>\fP\&. 
.br
 A \fBDeviceBuffer\fP behaves like a normal \fBCache\fP, but supports locking and shared‑memory synchronization for device kernels\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "class \fBDeviceSharedBuffer< TDeviceSharedBackend >\fP"
.br
.RI "Represents a shared memory bridge between a \fBDeviceBuffer\fP and a hardware‑specific backend implementing \fBIDeviceSharedBackend\fP\&. 
.br
 Manages the lifecycle of a hardware buffer, including creation, upload, download, and cleanup, depending on the configured \fBSharedCacheType\fP\&. "
.ti -1c
.RI "interface \fBIKernel< TIDeviceSharedBackend >\fP"
.br
.RI "Defines the interface for a compute kernel that operates on one or more \fBDeviceSharedBuffer<TDeviceSharedBackend>\fP instances\&. 
.br
 A kernel represents a unit of computation that may run on different backends such as RAM, OpenCL, Vulkan, CUDA, or custom hardware\&. "
